# VAPT PR Review Checklist

Use on every PR touching **auth, sessions, routes, controllers, uploads, or deployment security config**. The security-reviewer also runs it at Verify for any application change.

**PR title / link:** _______________
**Reviewer:** _______________
**Date:** _______________

**Always-on:** F4, F8, F9, F10. An applicable miss is **Critical**. N/A only when the diff cannot affect that control, with the reason.

**Regression:** F1, F2, F3, F5, F6, F7. HIGH and MEDIUM block merge when the diff touches that surface. LOW blocks only when the diff makes the issue exploitable. A route with no auth or authz is F4, not F5.

---

## F4 — Function-level access control (HIGH, always-on)

- [ ] The pack auth marker on every new or changed admin or mutation endpoint (`@PreAuthorize`, `[Authorize]`, a security `Depends()`, or Go auth middleware)
- [ ] Server-side route/module enforcement — not UI hide-only (web app)
- [ ] `app.security.permit-all` not enabled in lab/SIT/UAT/prod overlays
- [ ] No authz bypass flags in shared environments
- [ ] Policy or entitlement errors deny the request
- [ ] Test: restricted role → 403 on direct admin API/route access

---

## F8 — Object-level authorization (HIGH, always-on)

- [ ] Every `{id}` path authorizes that instance for the caller (tenant/org/user)
- [ ] Retest caller has the same role as the owner
- [ ] Writes bind through a DTO that rejects unknown properties
- [ ] Test: User A requests User B’s `{id}` → 403 or 404

---

## F9 — JWT validation (HIGH, always-on)

- [ ] Algorithm allowlist; `none` rejected
- [ ] `iss`, `aud`, `exp`, and `nbf` validated
- [ ] `kid` constrained to known keys
- [ ] Access-token lifetime short; refresh tokens rotate; reuse revokes the family
- [ ] Authorization identity is the validated `sub`
- [ ] Blacklist lookup fails closed
- [ ] Test: disallowed `alg`, wrong `aud` or `iss`, or expired token rejected

---

## F10 — Security audit events (MEDIUM, always-on)

- [ ] Auth success and failure, logout, authorization denial, token revocation, admin mutation, and upload accept/reject are logged
- [ ] Each event has correlation id, principal, action, and result
- [ ] Dynamic fields encoded; no token, password, or secret in the event
- [ ] Test: one denial and one admin or upload action

An applicable miss is Critical.

---

## F1 — Unauthorized Account Access (HIGH)

- [ ] Access token in memory; refresh token in an HttpOnly cookie
- [ ] Logout clears in-memory token, refresh cookie, and leftover client state
- [ ] User identity bound to validated JWT `sub`, not cached storage alone
- [ ] Server logout blacklists JWT, purges session Redis keys, revokes IdP session if SSO
- [ ] JWT blacklist fails closed on Redis/store errors
- [ ] Test: User A logout → User B login → User B everywhere

---

## F2 — Sensitive Info in Frontend (MEDIUM)

- [ ] No backend URLs, RBAC roles, or permission keys in client-bundled code
- [ ] No `PUBLIC_*` / `VITE_*` exposing internal config
- [ ] No demo/debug or config-leak routes in prod path
- [ ] `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` (correct value)
- [ ] Production sourcemaps disabled
- [ ] A secret, key, or personal-data leak is A04:2025; a debug or config leak is A02:2025

---

## F3 — File Upload Validation (MEDIUM)

- [ ] Server-side: size limit, content sniff (Tika/magic-byte), structure parse
- [ ] Generated storage name; `..` rejected; decompression limit; production virus scan
- [ ] Extension check is supplemental — not sole validation
- [ ] The pack auth marker on upload endpoints (`@PreAuthorize`, `[Authorize]`, a security `Depends()`, or Go auth middleware)
- [ ] Client `accept` is supplemental only (web app)
- [ ] Test: renamed wrong-type file → 400 before processing

---

## F5 — Exposed API Calls (LOW)

- [ ] A URL visible in the Network tab is informational
- [ ] A new route without auth or authz is recorded as F4, not F5
- [ ] No sensitive data in URL query strings
- [ ] Rate limits on auth/admin/upload paths where applicable

---

## F6 — Multiple Active Sessions (LOW)

- [ ] Session policy documented or prior tokens invalidated on login (if required)

---

## F7 — Cookies Without HttpOnly (LOW)

- [ ] New cookies: `httpOnly`, `secure` (prod), `sameSite` set
- [ ] No auth tokens via `document.cookie`
- [ ] An auth or refresh cookie missing a flag is a merge blocker

---

